WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.536
-Today the President
melted down yet again

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.038
in a Q&amp;A with reporters
after his White House

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:09.042
basically confessed to multiple
corrupt abuses of power.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.144
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.645
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.681
♪♪

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.818
We say this a lot,
but it was true again today.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.252
Donald Trump
talked to reporters,

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:21.854
and once again,
he lost his mind.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.924
In fact, you should just assume
that's always the case.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.460
His mind has always been lost.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.462
At this point,
it would be more shocking

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.231
if CNN told us
his mind had been found.

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.767 line:0%
"Breaking news --
Trump was normal today."

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:35.968 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.238
The President has always,
always been unhinged,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.205
and he's always hopped
from scandal to scandal.

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.842
But now, with the impeachment
inquiry intensifying,

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.211
it just feels like
more is happening faster.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.646
The Trump administration
right now

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.048
feels like
the "SportsCenter" of scandals.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.082
Instead of having to keep track

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:52.051
of a bunch of
different scandals,

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.586
like we did
for the first three years,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.721
now we're just getting
all the highlights

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.290
crammed together at once.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.459
"Trump just admitted
to a quid pro quo in D.C.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.593
And now we take you to New York,
where Aaron Rodgers

00:01:01.593 --> 00:01:04.296
just hit Rudy Giuliani
with a 38-yard touchdown pass

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:06.232
right in the [Bleep]."

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:10.603
So, as a result, there are
just more opportunities

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.005
for Trump to melt down
in public,

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.473
and that's what happened
again today.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.075
For example, Trump said
this insane thing

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.544
about his abrupt and
widely criticized decision

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.980
to abandon our Kurdish allies
in Syria

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.715
who have been fighting ISIS.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.617
-ISIS was all over the place.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:29.688
I'm the one -- meaning it was
me, and this administration --

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:33.059
working with others,
including the Kurds,

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.961
that captured
all of these people

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.563
that you're talking about
right now.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.499
Most of the ISIS fighters
that we captured --

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.002
we, we, not Obama, we --
We captured them, me.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.804
So I'm the one
that did the capturing.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.039
-No. No, you're not.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:49.141
You're not the one
who did the capturing.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:51.777
It makes it sound like he was
parachuting into Syria

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:54.246
on weekends like Tom Cruise
in "Mission: Impossible."

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:56.549
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.086
Trump also insisted once again

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.488
that his infamous phone call
with the president of Ukraine,

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:05.024
in which he dangled
hundreds of millions of dollars

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.592
in military aid
as part of a quid pro quo

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:09.562
to get Ukraine to manufacture
dirt on Joe Biden was perfect.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.732
But today he seemed to forget
that it was a phone call

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.199
and kept calling it a letter.

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:17.637
-This thing is all about
a letter that was perfect.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.606
You never hear the letter
anymore.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:21.941
The whistleblower's account was

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.543
totally different
than the letter.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.711
The whistleblower
gave a false account.

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.646
-The whistleblower
gave a false account?

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.049
You keep calling
a phone call a letter.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.451
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.085
Trump probably just changed it
in his mind

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.320
from a phone call to a letter

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.155
because he loves
getting letters.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.857
He's always
carrying them around

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:41.060
and waving them in the air,
showing them off to reporters.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.196
I mean, look at him.
He's like a high school senior

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:45.598
running into the house with
his college-acceptance letter.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:49.035
"Mom, look, Kim Jong-Un
loved my essay!"

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.269
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.205
Trump then had moved on...

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.473
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.342
Trump then moved on

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.678
to defending
his temporary decision

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.781
to hold next year's G7 summit
with world leaders

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.916
at his private golf course
in Florida,

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:05.217
which he rescinded on Saturday

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:06.785
after two days
of intense backlash.

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:08.988
Trump insisted
his golf course was

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.190
the perfect site
for an international summit.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.193
-Everybody in the G7 would have
had their own building.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.895
It was so good.
Florida loved it.

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:19.131
They love economic development.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:22.268
It -- It's not because --
It's a beautiful place.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.769
It's new.
It's been totally rebuilt.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:26.806
Everything's good.
Got massive meeting rooms.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:31.777
Unlimited security because it's
on, you know, hundreds of acres.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.713
Best location.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:36.883
Right next to the airport --
Miami International --

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.750
one of the biggest airports
in the world.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.219
Some people say
it's the biggest,

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.221
but one of the biggest airports
in the world.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.358
-What do you mean,
"Some say it's the biggest"?

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.827
It either is or --
It's not a mystery.

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:51.264
[ Laughter ]
We can measure it.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.566
And as a reporter noted
on Twitter,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.367
it's not even in the top 20.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.170
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.839
Trump...
[ Applause continues ]

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.208
I mean, Trump talks about it

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.877
like scientists have been
working for years

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.680
to discover which airport
is the biggest airport,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.282
like there are hieroglyphics
written on a cave somewhere

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:12.284
and archaeologists have been
trying to decipher them

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:13.552
in order to determine

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.187
whether Miami is one of
the biggest airports.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.423
"The symbols are a plane,
a plus sign,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.625
and a retiree
who lives in Palm Beach.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.961
What could it mean?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.463
Trump then defended himself
against accusations

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.599
that he was using the presidency
to rich himself

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:27.833
by lying about the fact

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.802
that he has no relationship with
his businesses,

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.837
and weirdly complaining
about a deal

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:34.973
President Obama made with
Netflix after he left office.

00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:36.475
-I don't run my business.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:38.911
I actually
put all the stuff in trusts.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.380
They run --
And I didn't have to do that.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.482
But under no obligation
to do it.

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:45.284
I don't know if you know it,
George Washington,

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.453
he ran his business
simultaneously

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:50.255
while he was President.
Many other Presidents --

00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:51.891
there weren't too many
really rich Presidents,

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.226
but there were a few --
they ran their business.

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:57.363
Hey, Obama made a deal
for a book.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.332
Is that running a business?
I'm sure

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:04.170
he didn't even discuss it
while he was President, yeah.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.704
He has a deal with Netflix.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:07.306
When did they start talking
about that?

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:10.642
-You think Obama was cutting
secret deals with Netflix

00:05:10.642 --> 00:05:12.878
during his presidency,

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.346
and we just
never heard about it?

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:16.749
You're the one who's constantly
talking about your golf courses.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.717
I never once heard Obama
end a press conference

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.352
by saying, [As Obama]
"And, uh, by the way,

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:22.054
if you, uh, like
what you heard today,

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:25.224
uh, check out
my new stand-up special

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.026
on Netflix.
It's called 'Barack Out.'"

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.894
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.196
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:33.633
[ Normal voice ] Then...
[ Applause continues ]

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.434
Then, Trump tried
a different argument.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:37.770
He defended himself by claiming
previous Presidents

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.606
also ran their businesses
while they were in office.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:45.178
-Other Presidents, if you look,
other Presidents were wealthy.

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:48.647
Not huge wealth.
George Washington was actually

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:51.250
considered a very, very rich man
at the time.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.319
But they ran their businesses.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:55.287
George Washington, they say,
had two desks.

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:57.423
He had a presidential desk
and a business desk.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.991
-Oh, is that what they say?

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.760
Are these also the same people

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.728
who say Miami is
the biggest airport?

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.229
[ Laughter ]
What business

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.699
was Washington supposedly
running on the side anyway?

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:07.900
[ As Trump ] Many people
don't know this,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.335
but George Washington
had a business

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.938
where he gave private boat tours
of the Delaware River.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.806
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.041
And on one phone, he'd be like,
"Uh, the British are coming."

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:17.476
And then he'd be like,
"We'd love to have your party

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:19.846
on our boat.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:21.848
Yeah, bring chips and stuff.

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:24.116
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.217
[ Normal voice ] And
you might remember,

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:26.485
that this all started
on Thursday,

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:28.120
when Trump's acting chief of
staff Mick Mulvaney

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.355
announced, out of nowhere,

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.123
that Trump had awarded
no big contract

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:34.226
to host a major
international summit to himself.

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:35.694
-We're going to announce today
that we're going to do

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:41.066
the 46th G7 summit,
on June 10th through June 12th,

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:44.970
at the Trump National Doral
facility in Miami, Florida.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.406
There's a long list of
the accommodations on site --

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:50.342
the ballrooms, bilateral rooms,

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:52.311
the number of rooms,
the photo ops,

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.079
the support hotels
that are there,

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:56.615
the proximity
to cities and airports,

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:59.752
helicopter landing zones,
medical facilities, et cetera.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:01.587
-Not only did he
just brazenly announce

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.022
that the President
would enrich himself

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:05.458
by hosting an official event
at his own golf course

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.660
but then he did
an infomercial for it.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.828
"There are ballrooms,
medical facilities,

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:11.130
helicopter landings.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.898
And if you book
for Halloween weekend,

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.400
you'll even meet
our creepy siblings."

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:19.672
Now Mulvaney...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:22.408
Mulvaney and Trump also insisted

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.176
the event wouldn't
actually benefit Trump,

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:27.580
because they would do it
at cost, or even for free.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.282
But this claim that Trump
would do it at cost

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:31.683
was obviously a sham,
because as we know,

00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:33.285
from previous events
at Trump resorts,

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:34.686
that's not how it works.

00:07:34.686 --> 00:07:37.256
For example, at previous events
at Trump properties,

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:41.126
taxpayers have paid $546 a night
for hotel rooms at Mar-a-Lago

00:07:41.126 --> 00:07:42.995
and $1,000 for liquor

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.064
that White House staffers drank
in one sitting.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:47.866
The only way spending $1,000
for liquor in one sitting

00:07:47.866 --> 00:07:50.102
makes sense is if you are
a White House staffer.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.737
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.639
"The other day he called the FBI

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.775
because he couldn't find
his remote control."

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:58.711
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.746
We're all gonna die in jail."

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:02.215
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:03.749
I'm sorry, but if taxpayers

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.183
are gonna spend 1,000 bucks
on booze,

00:08:05.183 --> 00:08:07.152
then they should get to drink
the booze themselves,

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:08.687
especially if we have to deal
with this President.

00:08:08.687 --> 00:08:11.590
In fact, every Trump tweet
should come with an option

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.825
to retweet, like, or, "Send me
a bottle of whiskey."

00:08:13.825 --> 00:08:15.494
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:18.330
So, after the outcry,

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.299
Trump rescinded the decision
on Twitter,

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:23.034
and then Mulvaney had to
go on the Sunday shows

00:08:23.034 --> 00:08:25.838
to explain why Trump was
so wounded by all the backlash.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.808
-He was honestly surprised
at the level of pushback.

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:31.444
At the end of the day, you know,
he still considers himself

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:33.446
to be in
the hospitality business.

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:35.581
-Okay, first of all, he's not
in the hospitality business.

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:36.915
He's the President.

00:08:36.915 --> 00:08:39.785
Second, Trump was never
in the hospitality business.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.787
Hospitality is when
you show warmth

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:44.090
and compassion
to guests and strangers.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.025
Trump was in the "ruthless
real-estate ass[Bleep]

00:08:46.025 --> 00:08:48.194
who stands like a baboon
on his hind legs" business.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:50.496
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:53.165
But this is such...
[ Applause ]

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:56.635
This is such a key confession
from Mulvaney

00:08:56.635 --> 00:08:59.004
because it explains so much.
Trump still sees himself

00:08:59.004 --> 00:09:01.506
as the corrupt real estate mogul
and reality star

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:02.975
who always got away with
whatever he wanted,

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.576
rather than
a government official

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:05.944
who's bound to the rule of law.

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:07.780
That's the Trump we saw
in that infamous phone call

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:08.981
with the president of Ukraine.

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.683
And during his press conference
on Thursday,

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:12.151
Mulvaney literally admitted

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.985
that they held up
the aid to Ukraine

00:09:13.985 --> 00:09:16.455
as part of a quid pro quo
to investigate the Democrats.

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:17.990
-Did he also mention to me,
in past,

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.193
the corruption related
to the DNC server?

00:09:21.193 --> 00:09:23.062
Absolutely,
no question about that.

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:25.230
But that's it, and that's
why we held up the money.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.800
Now, there was a report -- -
-So, the demand

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.869
for an investigation
into the Democrats

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:31.436
was part of the reason
that he --

00:09:31.436 --> 00:09:34.006
in order to withhold
funding to Ukraine?

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:37.610
-The look back
to what happened in 2016

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.912
certainly was part of the thing
that he was worried about

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:41.247
and corruption with that nation,

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:42.648
and that is
absolutely appropriate.

00:09:42.648 --> 00:09:44.082
-Withholding the funding?
-Yeah.

00:09:44.082 --> 00:09:46.585
-But, to be clear, what you
described is a quid pro quo.

00:09:46.585 --> 00:09:50.122
It is, "Funding will not flow
unless the investigation

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:54.627
into the Democratic server
happened, as well."

00:09:54.627 --> 00:09:57.029
-We do -- We do that
all the time

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:59.398
with foreign policy.
-You do?!

00:09:59.398 --> 00:10:02.268
[ Laughter ]
So, not only did he admit it,

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:05.304
he said this isn't even
the only time they've done it.

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:07.039
In fact, many people
don't know this,

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.907
but, uh, Washington
had two desks --

00:10:08.907 --> 00:10:11.076
one for business
and one for crime.

00:10:11.076 --> 00:10:13.345
Mulvaney got even more brazen,

00:10:13.345 --> 00:10:15.814
openly bragging about the scheme
and saying this.

00:10:15.814 --> 00:10:17.917
-I have news for everybody.
Get over it.

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:21.086
There's going to be political
influence in foreign policy.

00:10:21.086 --> 00:10:22.754
-"Get over it?"
I'm sorry,

00:10:22.754 --> 00:10:25.124
but you don't get to talk
about an illegal quid pro quo

00:10:25.124 --> 00:10:26.926
that's at the center
of an impeachment inquiry

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:29.628
like you're a cartoon mom
on a funny T-shirt.

00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:31.497
"5:00 is wine o'clock,
and if you don't like it,

00:10:31.497 --> 00:10:33.165
you can build a bridge
and get over it."

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:37.269
Mulvaney continued to argue
that the President was allowed

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:39.037
to do whatever he wants
in foreign policy

00:10:39.037 --> 00:10:41.607
and allowed to use
whoever he wants to do it,

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:43.375
like his personal lawyer,
Rudy Giuliani,

00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:45.444
who is reportedly
under criminal investigation.

00:10:45.444 --> 00:10:47.579
-Do you believe
that Rudy Giuliani's role

00:10:47.579 --> 00:10:49.414
as an outside adviser
to the President

00:10:49.414 --> 00:10:51.951
is problematic?
-That's the President's call.

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:54.420
The President
gets to set foreign policy,

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.821
and he gets to choose
who to do so,

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:57.490
as long as it doesn't
violate any law.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.391
-Okay, but it probably did.

00:10:59.391 --> 00:11:02.060
I mean, two of Rudy's associates
who helped him

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.362
dig up dirt in Ukraine
have already been arrested.

00:11:04.362 --> 00:11:07.500
Remember these two
Halloween decorations?

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.567
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:10.802
Lev and Igor, their real names?

00:11:10.802 --> 00:11:13.538
I mean, the guys who look like
they just got arrested

00:11:13.538 --> 00:11:16.175
for huffing
bowling-alley shoe spray?

00:11:16.175 --> 00:11:19.144
The mobster versions
of Bill and Ted.

00:11:19.144 --> 00:11:21.112
They've been in multiple photos

00:11:21.112 --> 00:11:22.414
with Rudy, Trump,
and Mike Pence.

00:11:22.414 --> 00:11:24.116
And you can't forget them
because they look like

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:26.218
they should be hanging out
with rocky and Mugsy.

00:11:26.218 --> 00:11:28.020
[ Laughter ]

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.254
So, now Mulvaney's confession,

00:11:29.254 --> 00:11:31.256
which comes after
Trump's own confession,

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:33.391
let's remember, has left
the rest of the administration

00:11:33.391 --> 00:11:34.560
struggling with how to respond.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.161
Yesterday, Secretary of State
Mike Pompeo,

00:11:36.161 --> 00:11:38.463
who's also implicated
in this whole scheme,

00:11:38.463 --> 00:11:40.699
was asked about
Mulvaney's comments on ABC.

00:11:40.699 --> 00:11:43.502
And you can see his brain
short-circuit in real time.

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:45.103
-What I'm asking is,
would it be appropriate

00:11:45.103 --> 00:11:46.739
to condition that aid?
-George, I'm not going to

00:11:46.739 --> 00:11:48.941
get into hypotheticals and
secondary things

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:50.576
based on what
someone else has said.

00:11:50.576 --> 00:11:51.977
George, you would have
never done it

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:53.979
when you were the spokesman.
I'm not going to do it here.

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:56.782
-Well, it's not a hypothetical.
We saw the chief of staff.

00:11:56.782 --> 00:11:58.484
-It is, George.
You just said "if."

00:11:58.484 --> 00:12:00.919
George, you just said
"if this happened."

00:12:00.919 --> 00:12:02.922
That is, by definition,
a hypothetical.

00:12:02.922 --> 00:12:04.490
-The chief of staff said it did.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:07.059
[ Laughter ]

00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:09.328
-George, you asked me
"if this happened."

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:10.896
It's a hypothetical.
-Wow.

00:12:10.896 --> 00:12:12.564
Normally, when someone
takes that long

00:12:12.564 --> 00:12:16.001
to answer a question on TV,
a red "X" pops up on-screen.

00:12:16.001 --> 00:12:17.336
[ Laughter ]

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:18.704
Top five answers on the board.

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:21.640
Name a country
the President has colluded with.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.608
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.608 --> 00:12:25.310
[ Buzzer ]

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.413
Sorry.
[ Applause ]

00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:29.882
The answer we were looking for
was Ukraine.

00:12:29.882 --> 00:12:32.985
[ Applause ]
Ukraine.

00:12:32.985 --> 00:12:34.419
[ Laughter ]

00:12:34.419 --> 00:12:36.622
Things are moving very fast
for Trump and his henchmen,

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:38.223
and that's because
the impeachment inquiry

00:12:38.223 --> 00:12:39.858
has finally provided
a political process

00:12:39.858 --> 00:12:41.259
to hold them accountable.

00:12:41.259 --> 00:12:42.928
I don't know if any of these
guys will ever be arrested,

00:12:42.928 --> 00:12:45.131
but if they are, I hope
the cops who do it say...

00:12:45.131 --> 00:12:47.165
-I'm the one
that did the capturing.

00:12:47.165 --> 00:12:48.934
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:48.934 --> 00:12:50.936
[ Cheers and applause ]

